    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0024" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/5–150: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to All Diplomatic Missions and
                        Certain Consular Offices </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d5-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-05-01T10:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1950—10 a.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dept interested receiving regular reports on press and other public reaction
                    abroad to Hoover<anchor n="2" xml:id="d5-f2"/> proposal for org of UN without
                    the participation of Commie countries.</p>
                <p>Dept desires initial report soonest.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d5-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Transmitted for info only to AmEmb Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d5-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d5-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to all Embassies and Legations; to the High Commissioner, Germany; to
                    the United States Political Adviser, Tokyo; and to consular officers at Algiers,
                    Dakar, Hong Kong, Singapore, Taipei, Tripoli, and Rabat.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f2" n="2" xml:id="d5-f2-content">
                <p>Ex-President Herbert Hoover.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f3" n="3" xml:id="d5-f3-content">
                <p>Relevant documentation is located in the 310.2 file.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
